# Docker semantics, not gitignore: patterns are relative to the repo root and a bare name matches
# only at the root. Hence the `**/` prefixes for names that can appear in any workspace.

# Version control and local tooling
.git
.gitignore
**/.claude
**/.vscode
**/.idea

# Dependencies and build output: the image runs `npm ci` and `npm run build` itself
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.angular
*/out-tsc
*/coverage
coverage

# Local data. The SQLite database, its WAL files and backups must never end up in an image.
# The folders are anchored on purpose: a source folder such as backend/src/modules/backups must stay.
data
backend/data
backups
backend/backups
**/*.db
**/*.db-*
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite-*
**/*.sqlite3

# Local configuration and secrets
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Tests and test artifacts (nothing here is part of the build)
**/*.test.ts
**/*.spec.ts
**/e2e
**/playwright-report
**/test-results
**/blob-report

# Docs, Docker files and editor/OS files: they only bust the build cache
docs
**/*.md
Dockerfile*
docker-compose*.yml
compose*.yml
.dockerignore
.editorconfig
.nvmrc
.prettierrc
.prettierignore
**/*.log
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
